<title>FRANCE: French February raw steel output up 15.4 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>French February raw steel output up 15.4 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French raw steel output jumped 15.4 percent to 1.502 million tonnes in February 1997 over February 1996, statistics from the French steel federation showed.</p>
<p>In a statement the federation said the rise reflected an upturn in steel demand in Europe.</p>
<p>Output for the first two months of 1997 reached 3.001 million tonnes, up 12.8 percent over the same period for 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
